  "result": {
    "text": "def add_elements(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a non-empty-empty array ` arr` and an integer `k`, return the total sum of the elements\n with at most two digits from the first k elements of arr.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i  in arr:\n        if len(str(i)) <= 10:\n            total_sum += i\n    return total_sum\n\n# Example usage:\nprint(add_elements([111,21,3,4000,5,6,7,8,9], 4)) # Expected Output: 24",
